        "name": "Escaping",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The term is percent-encoded with the built-in `urllib.parse.quote(term, safe=\"\")` inside the href, and both the full URL and the visible text are escaped with `html.escape`, so inputs like `\"><script>x</script>` or `a&b=c` cannot break out of either context; a test confirms this for a hostile input."
      },
      {
        "name": "Behavior",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "It returns exactly one `<a>` pointing to `https://help.example.com/search?q=<encoded term>` with the visible text `Search the help center for <term>`, and tests cover both a plain and a hostile term."
